"""Q23: add Q23 entries to /output/report.json (idempotent). Usage: python3 -I s144_update_report_q23.py"""
import json
p='/output/report.json'; d=json.load(open(p)); R=d['results']
R[:]=[x for x in R if not x['quantity'].startswith('Q23:')]
d['recipe']=[x for x in d['recipe'] if not x['description'].startswith('Q23:')]
d['caveats']=[x for x in d['caveats'] if not x.startswith('Q23:')]
A=lambda n,v:{'name':n,'value':v}
v=("Round-2 result (velocity convention corrected: radio velocity, the LOW-frequency spw edge is the RED (+v) side, so the ramp is a red-side deficit that runs into the red wing of the +-350 km/s window). "
 "The ramp biases the ladder integrals and ratios by less than 1 sigma at N, S, Bridge, but for HCN 4-3 the raw integral is LOW by ~+3..+10% if the ramp persists under the red wing. "
 "Evidence the ramp exists in the ladder spws (peak pixel, N+S+Bridge stack, amplitude as fraction of continuum): Xb55 spw18 (HCO+ 2-1) -0.13..-0.15+-0.03; Xb4f spw18 (HCN 3-2) -0.10+-0.03; Xb47 spw16 (HCN 4-3) -0.08+-0.02 (delta-chi2 ~19 vs no ramp); controls consistent with zero: Xb55 spw16 (HCN 2-1) -0.03+-0.02, Xb4f spw16 (HCO+ 3-2) -0.05+-0.02 (marginal), Xb47 spw18 (HCO+ 4-3) -0.01+-0.01; Xb4d/Xb4b no ramp. "
 "Direct test (observed blue[-600..-420] minus red[+420..+600] level, mJy/channel, N+S+Bridge, vs the fitted continuum-scaled ramp model, in-sample / leave-one-region-out): Xb55 spw18 +2.15+-0.53 observed vs +1.62 / +1.61 predicted (chi2 2.4/3 vs 18/3 for no ramp); Xb4f spw18 +0.87+-0.39 vs +1.28 / +1.36 (2.6/3 vs 5.7/3); Xb47 spw16 +1.06+-0.66 vs +1.95 / +1.83 (2.3/3 vs 4.1/3); no-ramp controls: Xb55 spw16 +0.41+-0.40 vs 0.03, Xb4f spw16 -0.28+-0.52 vs +0.71, Xb47 spw18 +0.02+-0.53 vs 0; Xb4d/Xb4b HCN 3-2 -0.00+-0.11 / -0.05+-0.06. The red-side deficit is therefore the ramp itself (right sign, right spws, continuum-proportional at N/S/Bridge), not an independent baseline error; the previous reading (blue-side ramp, 'opposite sign', separate 5-12% systematic) was wrong and is withdrawn. "
 "Shape: in the measured profiles (s146) the ramp does not die in the first ~10 channels in the ladder spws: Xb47 spw16 is a plateau of ~-0.07+-0.02 x cont out to the window start (ch 48; a MHz-scaled Xb55 empirical shape that ends by ch~45 predicts 0), Xb4f spw18 -0.10 x cont to ch ~60 (window starts ch 74), Xb55 spw18 -0.09+-0.05 at the window start (ch 76). I therefore take the ramp to extend into the red wing (triangle c0=200-400 ch) as the realistic case and the short empirical/exponential/c0<=100 shapes as the optimistic bound. "
 "Integral change when the fitted ramp is removed (E0 = s30 estimator; optimistic [short ramp] .. realistic [tri200-400]): HCN 4-3 N -1.9..+2.6..+6.6%, S -3.2..+2.8..+9.7%, Bridge -1.1..+3.9..+8.7% (stat 1.8, 3.9, 3.1%; +-7% calibration; the raw HCN 4-3 integral is too LOW, not too high: the ramp under the red wing outweighs its depression of the red baseline channels); HCN 3-2 -0.3..+1.3..+2.8% (N), +1.8..+3.3 (S), +1.1..+2.9 (Bridge); HCO+ 2-1 <=+1.4%; HCN 2-1, HCO+ 3-2, HCO+ 4-3: <=+0.5% (no ramp / outside window). "
 "Ratio shifts, optimistic .. tri400: HCN/HCO+ 2-1 0..-1.3% ; 3-2 0..+2.5% ; 4-3 N -1.9..+6.3%, S -3.2..+10.2%, Bridge -1.1..+8.4% (largest 0.95 sigma at S, the ratio error is ~10% = stat + 7% calibration per line); HCN T43/T32 N -1.6..+3.7%, S -2.9..+6.2%, Bridge -0.7..+5.7% (<=0.6 sigma); HCN T21/T32 0..-3.2%; HCO+ ladder ratios <=0.5%. The N/S contrast in HCN T43/T32 (p0022) changes by <=2.5% (ramp scales with continuum at both). No ladder result moves beyond 1 sigma; the HCN 4-3-based ratios should be quoted as raw +4+-4% (N), +6+-5% (S), +6+-4% (Bridge) up, i.e. HCN/HCO+ 4-3 and T43/T32 are biased low in the old tables. "
 "Ramp-immune cross-check (baseline from the blue side only, v<-450, same +-350 window; the ramp under the red wing is NOT removed by any baseline choice, only the template can address it): E1 vs s30 shifts HCN/HCO+ and ladder ratios by <=0.2 sigma everywhere except HCO+ 4-3 at S (+6.8%, a baseline structure on the blue side, not the ramp: control spw without ramp), which moves HCO+ T43/T32 at S by +6.3% (0.6 sigma) and HCN/HCO+ 4-3 at S by -5.6% (0.5 sigma). A blue-side linear baseline over -900<v<-450 is unstable (HCO+ 4-3 S 28.4 vs 20.3 Jy/beam km/s; slope noise from the long lever arm) and a +-250 km/s window changes integrals by line wings (<=3%), neither is a ramp test; the baseline-choice spread (E0/E1/E3) is <=2% for all ladder lines except HCO+ 4-3 S. "
 "W (HCN 4-3 non-detection 0.05+-0.30 Jy/beam km/s) and E1/E2 are not quoted in percent: absolute ramp shift for W <=0.03-0.1 Jy/beam km/s (<0.3 sigma); E1/E2 have too little continuum for a ramp (E1 7 mJy at Xb55: <=1 mJy ramp, <=1.5% of HCO+ 2-1). Ramp extent under the line wing (v=+250..+350 km/s, the same channels as the red ridge of p0017/p0018) is not measurable and is the dominant uncertainty; not tested on matched-beam cubes (ramp ~ fraction of beam-convolved continuum, so fractions carry over).")
R.append({'quantity':'Q23: bias of HCN/HCO+ 2-1, 3-2, 4-3 integrals, HCN/HCO+ ratios and ladder ratios from the continuum-proportional spw low-edge ramp','target':'Xb55, Xb4f, Xb47 (and Xb4d, Xb4b) at N, S, Bridge, W, (E1, E2)','value':v,
 'uncertainty':'HCN 4-3 integral +3..+10% low (range = ramp extent under the red wing, 1-2 x the stat error, +-7% calibration); HCN 3-2 <=+3%; HCO+ 2-1 <=1.4%; ratio shifts <=0.95 sigma (HCN/HCO+ 4-3 at S), <=0.6 sigma for ladder ratios','unit':'percent of integral; sigma',
 'assumptions':[A('ramp shape','amplitude f x s131 continuum fitted jointly on N,S,Bridge line-free red channels (v>+380 km/s); shapes triangle c0=50-400 ch, exponential, Xb55-empirical; red side = low-frequency edge'),A('continuum','s131 line-free continuum at each region pixel and OUS beam; E1/E2 not modelled'),A('spectra','native-beam peak-pixel and aperture spectra, not the matched-beam cubes; the ramp is a fraction of the (beam-convolved) continuum, so fractions carry over to matched beams to within the continuum smoothing'),A('error','ratio total error = stat + 2 x 7% calibration')],
 'confidence':'medium','evidence':'scripts/s145_q23_redo.py, s146_q23_profiles.py, s147_q23_direct_summary.py (round 2; out/q23/s145-s147.txt) and s140-s143 (round 1; velocity direction in their text is wrong, numbers superseded where they differ)'})
d['recipe'].append({'description':'Q23: ladder-line positions vs spw edges (s140), first-pass ramp fit and MC (s141-s143; direction mislabelled there), round 2: red-side direct test, shape comparison, blue-only baseline estimators, ramp-template corrections (s145), measured edge profiles (s146), pooled summary (s147), report (s144)','scripts':[f'/workspace/scripts/{k}.py' for k in ('s140_q23_line_edges','s141_q23_line_bias','s142_q23_bias_mc','s143_q23_summary','s145_q23_redo','s146_q23_profiles','s147_q23_direct_summary','s144_update_report_q23')],'order':max(x['order'] for x in d['recipe'])+1,'stage':d['recipe'][-1]['stage']})
d['caveats'].append("Q23: the low-frequency-edge (RED-side) ramp is real in Xb55 spw18, Xb4f spw18 and Xb47 spw16 and persists as a plateau of ~-0.07..-0.10 x continuum to the window start, so it lowers the HCN 4-3 integral by ~3-10% (HCN 3-2 <=3%, HCO+ 2-1 <=1.4%); HCN/HCO+ 4-3 and HCN T43/T32 in earlier tables are biased low by up to ~10% and ~6% (<1 sigma). The N/S contrast is unchanged. Extent of the ramp under the red wing (+250..+350 km/s) is unconstrained by the data.")
json.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=1)
